===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnˈhɛɹətəns/}}
* {{audio|En-us-inheritance.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Etymology===
Recorded since 1473, from to [[inherit]], itself from {{etyl|fro|en}} [[enheriter]] "make heir, appoint as heir," from {{etyl|LL.|en}} [[inhereditare]] "to appoint as heir," from {{etyl|la|en}} [[in-]] "in" + [[hereditare]] "to inherit," from [[heres]] (gen. heredis) "heir".

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The passing of [[title]] to an [[estate]] upon death.
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} That which a person is entitled to [[inherit]], by law or [[testament]].
# (biology) The [[hereditary]] passing of biological [[attribute]]s from ancestors to their [[offspring]].
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} In object-oriented programming, the mechanism whereby parts of a [[superclass]] are available to instances of its [[subclass]].

